    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the probability that four fair 6-sided dice will not all show the same number, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of possible outcomes when rolling four dice:**\n   Each die has 6 faces, and since the dice are rolled independently, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   6^4 = 1296\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of favorable outcomes where all four dice show the same number:**\n   There are 6 possible outcomes where all four dice show the same number (i.e., all showing 1, all showing 2, ..., all showing 6). So, there are 6 favorable outcomes.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of outcomes where not all four dice show the same number:**\n   This is the total number of possible outcomes minus the number of unfavorable outcomes:\n   \\[\n   1296 - 6 = 1290\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the probability that not all four dice show the same number:**\n   The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1290}{1296} = \\frac{215}{216}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the four dice will not all show the same number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{215}{216}}\n\\]",
