      "text": "When we roll the two identical dice, the probability that they both show (1, 1).\n$\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right) = \\frac{1}{36}$.\n\nFor the remaining two dice, the probability that they do not both show (1, 1) is $1 - \\frac{1}{36} = \\frac{35}{36}$.\n\nTherefore, the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show (the same number) is $2\\left(\\frac{35}{36}\\right)^2$.\n\nThus, the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same is \\boxed{\\frac{245}{1296}}.",
